# /etc/rt-engine/env — created by engine/install-units.sh from the live
# agent environment. NEVER commit real values anywhere.
#
# Why this file exists: this VM egresses through a proxy. Python urllib
# clients (monitor.py, settle.py, hl_cache.py) pick the proxy up from these
# environment variables automatically. systemd services start with a clean
# environment, so without this file every fetch fails with
# "SSL: WRONG_VERSION_NUMBER" (direct TLS egress is broken on this VM).
# engine/lib.sh sources this file at the top of every module runner.
#
# Variables captured (values come from the environment at install time):
#   http_proxy https_proxy HTTP_PROXY HTTPS_PROXY
#   ALL_PROXY all_proxy no_proxy NO_PROXY
#
# After a VM replacement the proxy credential may rotate; if module fetches
# start failing with WRONG_VERSION_NUMBER again, re-run install-units.sh
# from an agent shell to refresh this file.
